course: dictionary
lesson: 10443
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words around it, which is its context. «Truffle» is a word like this.
explain: «The box held six chocolate truffles, each dusted with cocoa powder.» Here a truffle is a sweet. «Pigs have been used to find truffles, a mushroom that grows underground.» Here a truffle is a fungus. The clues are chocolate and cocoa in the first sentence, and grows underground in the second.
explain: Check your choice by swapping in the meaning. Does «a mushroom that grows underground» fit in the box of chocolates? No. Does «a soft chocolate sweet» fit when pigs are sniffing for something? No. The meaning that makes sense is the right one.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so always read the whole sentence.
fact: «Truffle» can mean a soft, round chocolate sweet, often covered in cocoa powder.
fact: «Truffle» can also mean a rare, strong-smelling fungus that grows underground near tree roots.
fact: Truffles are very expensive to eat, and they are among the most expensive foods in the world.
fact: Pigs and specially trained dogs sniff out truffles; many hunters now use dogs, because pigs eat them.
exercise: «The box held six chocolate truffles.» What is a truffle in this sentence? | *A soft, round chocolate sweet | A pig's snout | A rare fungus that grows underground | A kind of tree root
exercise: «Pigs have been used to find truffles, a mushroom that grows underground.» What does truffle mean here? | A chocolate sweet covered in cocoa | A box of gifts | *A rare fungus that grows underground | A flat disc on a pig's snout
exercise: Jade reads «truffle dog» and says it is a dog that likes chocolate sweets. What does «truffle dog» most likely mean? | A dog with a cocoa powder coat | A dog that sleeps in a box | *A dog trained to sniff out truffles | A dog that eats chocolate sweets
test: «Truffles are very rare.» What does rare mean here? | Very cheap | Found in every shop | *Not found very often | Made of plastic
test: In «The box held six chocolate truffles, each dusted with cocoa powder», which words tell you the truffle is a sweet? | Pigs and dogs | Six and box | *Chocolate and cocoa powder | Underground and tree roots
exam: «Dogs were trained to sniff out truffles that grew underground.» What is a truffle in this sentence? | A box of cocoa powder | *A fungus that grows underground | A soft chocolate sweet | A kind of pig
